            <ArticleTitle>[Cecum mobility as a cause of ileus].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>568-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present a rare case of ileus caused by unusual cecum mobility. The 31-years old female patient was diagnosed ineffectively several times due to abdominal pain. The diagnostics, an attempt of a conservative treatment, along with surgical and postoperative treatment are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
